From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:10:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Refuse to derive an image from a surface the scaler
 shrank

vaDeriveImage() maps a surface's memory for the CPU. A surface the
decode-time scaler wrote (V4L2_REQUEST_SCALE) holds fewer pixels than
the client created it for, 1920x1080 in a 3840x2160 surface. The derived
image described that (the smaller of surface and memory), and vaGetImage
already refused such a surface, but the clients that map do not read the
image's size: they size the copy from the surface. Measured on the H713
(package D, T2): GStreamer va's system-memory path copied 3840 bytes per
line out of a 1920-pitch mapping, read about 1 MB past its end, crashed
with SIGSEGV after five frames into fakesink and wrote a broken last
frame before EOS into a file; FFmpeg's hwmap gives the frame the pool's
size and only stayed in bounds with an explicit crop. Wrong pixels or a
crash instead of an error.

Refuse it, as vaGetImage does: whenever the memory behind a surface is
smaller than the surface, vaDeriveImage fails with
VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED (a trace line under LIBVA_V4L2_TRACE
says why). Without scaling this cannot happen: decoders pad their
buffers up, never down, and backing for bare surfaces is allocated at
least at the surface's size. The export (vaExportSurfaceHandle) is
unchanged and keeps describing the real size; a GPU importer that asks
for more checks the buffer itself (Panfrost: EGL_BAD_ALLOC).

License: GPL-3.0-or-later, like the code it changes (libva-v4l2_request).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/image.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/image.c b/src/image.c
index 0601f27..c408b22 100644
--- a/src/image.c
+++ b/src/image.c
@@ -164,6 +164,23 @@ static VAStatus derive_image(VADriverContextP va_ctx, VASurfaceID surface_id,
 	if (view.nb_planes != 1 || view.info->lsb_shift)
 		return VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED;
 
+	/*
+	 * Nor when the memory holds fewer pixels than the surface was created
+	 * for: a surface the decode-time scaler wrote (V4L2_REQUEST_SCALE).
+	 * The image would describe that honestly, but the clients that map
+	 * surfaces size the copy from the surface: GStreamer va copied a
+	 * 3840x2160 picture out of a 1920x1080 mapping, read past its end
+	 * and crashed, FFmpeg's hwmap keeps the frame at the pool's size.
+	 * Refuse, like vaGetImage does; the export describes the real size.
+	 */
+	if (view.width < surface->width || view.height < surface->height) {
+		v4l2r_trace("derive surface 0x%08x refused: created %ux%u, "
+			    "memory %ux%u (scaled)\n", surface->id,
+			    surface->width, surface->height, view.width,
+			    view.height);
+		return VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED;
+	}
+
 	pthread_mutex_lock(&drv->mutex);
 	image_id = v4l2r_handles_alloc(&drv->images, sizeof(*image_object));
 	image_object = V4L2R_IMAGE(drv, image_id);
-- 
